VCDecTest - the vcdec library on the Raspberry Pi
================================================

vcdec is the library Reel and FFmpeg will use to have H.264 decoded by the
VideoCore, through RISC OS's VCHIQ module. It does what MMALDecode 0.12 to
0.17 found works, behind five calls: open, send an access unit with its
time, take a picture, flush (for a seek), close. Nothing in it waits for
the decoder except open, flush and close, so a player can drive it from
Wimp null events.

VCDecTest drives it as a player would: each turn it sends access units
until vcdec says the decoder's input is full, then takes every picture
that's ready. Each picture is copied into the program's own memory and
checked against a checksum FFmpeg made of the same picture, matched by
its time (pts). The VideoCore's pictures can differ from FFmpeg's by 1 in
a few values (rounding), so each is also compared by block averages:
"within rounding" is fine, anything more is a fault.

New in vcdec, not tried on the Pi before:
  - the pictures' bulk transfers run on while the next messages are
    handled, instead of being waited for one by one (Sync waits, as
    MMALDecode did, to compare);
  - a seek after the end of the stream creates the decoder again (a flush
    alone lost the last two pictures in MMALDecode's SeekE): SeekEnd.

The clips (in clips, the same as MMALDecode 0.17's):
  small  640x360, 60 pictures, H.264 Main with B frames, a keyframe
         every 20
  odd    426x240, 30 pictures, H.264 Baseline (a width that isn't a
         multiple of 32, to check the cropping)
  hd     1920x1080, 150 pictures, H.264 High, level 4.1, B frames

Running it (please send back every Result file):
  Test     The three clips, every picture checked. Writes Result.
  Sync     As Test, each bulk transfer waited for. Writes ResultSync.
  Seek     The small clip; after 10 pictures a flush, then on from the
           keyframe at picture 40, before the end of the stream was sent.
           Every message written out. Writes ResultSeek.
  SeekEnd  The small and hd clips, each to the end, then a flush (the
           decoder created again) and on from the last keyframe to the end
           again. Writes ResultEnd.
  Speed    The three clips without checks: pictures a second, with each
           one copied out; then hd again as Sync. Writes ResultT.
  Verbose  The small clip with every message (ResultV), if Test doesn't
           get pictures back.

  Each report says how much memory the VideoCore has (gpu_mem in
  CONFIG/TXT). 1080p needs gpu_mem=128 or more: vcdec won't open the hd
  clip below that (at 64 the decoder stalls without a word).

If a run stops part way (the report says "no reply"), the VideoCore's
decoder can stay stuck until the machine is restarted: restart before
running anything else. If the machine locks up (it shouldn't), switch it
off and on again.

Needs: RISC OS 5 on a Raspberry Pi, with the VCHIQ module (in the ROM).
Part of riscos-reelhwaccel; GPL version 2 or later. The clips are made
from FFmpeg's testsrc2 pattern.
